        <article id="orient" class="help-chapter">
            <h2>Orient</h2>

            <section id="start-here" class="help-section">
                <h3>Start here</h3>
                <p>KeyInventory helps a key custodian maintain <strong>KEY #</strong> access patterns and the <strong>Room #</strong> values each KEY # opens, register <strong>MEDECO</strong> physical copies under a KEY #, issue and return exact copies to people, see who currently holds each copy, correct authorized records, and review audit history and reports.</p>
                <p>Departments and Rooms belong directly to this installation. Home is the operational dashboard; open Help when you need reference guidance.</p>
                <div class="help-diagram-note"><strong>Example:</strong> KEY # <code>66800</code> opens Room <code>410D</code>. Physical copies MEDECO <code>26</code>, <code>27</code>, and <code>28</code> share that access. Issue and return always name the exact MEDECO copy — for example KEY # 66800 / MEDECO 26 — not merely the KEY #.</div>
            </section>

            <section id="organized" class="help-section">
                <h3>How KeyInventory is organized</h3>
                <p>Use the primary navigation for daily work:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Home</strong> — operational dashboard: custody metrics and recent activity.</li>
                    <li><strong>Operations</strong> — Issue Key, Receive Key, Active Loans, History, Find Key.</li>
                    <li><strong>Catalog</strong> — Keys, Key Types, Register Key, KEY # Rooms.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reports</strong> — read-only views with CSV, Excel, and PDF export.</li>
                    <li><strong>Administration</strong> — Departments, Rooms, Workforce Members, Work Assignments, Audit Trail.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>When a capability’s prerequisites are missing, the page explains what is still required and links to resolve it. Home stays an operational dashboard — not a permanent setup wizard.</p>
            </section>

