        <article id="configure" class="help-chapter">
            <h2>Configure</h2>

            <section id="departments-rooms" class="help-section">
                <h3>Departments &amp; rooms</h3>
                <p><strong>Departments</strong> name organizational units used for membership and department-based issue justification. The <strong>department code</strong> is what you type and may edit; the system keeps a stable internal department identity you never need to manage.</p>
                <p><strong>Rooms</strong> define places for work assignments and rooms opened by keys. <strong>Room #</strong> is operator-facing and editable; the system assigns a stable internal room identity automatically. Room numbers are unique across the whole installation.</p>
                <div class="help-links">
                    <a asp-page="/Administration/Departments/Index">Departments</a>
                    <a asp-page="/Administration/Rooms/Index">Rooms</a>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="workforce" class="help-section">
                <h3>Workforce &amp; assignments</h3>
                <p><strong>Workforce Member</strong> is the person represented in workforce administration. Each member needs an active department. No second member is required to add the first person.</p>
                <p><strong>Work Assignment</strong> is the governed current relationship used by issue eligibility (member ↔ room). An active assignment is <strong>mandatory before Issue Key</strong>.</p>
                <p><strong>Key holder</strong> is an operational role while an eligible person holds a physical MEDECO copy — not a separate record type you administer.</p>
                <div class="help-diagram-frame" role="img" aria-label="Workforce model: Workforce Member to Work Assignment to eligible holder to physical key custody">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 640 130" width="640" height="130" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
