                        <rect x="160" y="44" width="120" height="40" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="220" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Work Assignment</text>
                        <rect x="304" y="44" width="140" height="40" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="374" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Eligible holder</text><text x="374" y="76" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="8">(Issue search)</text>
                        <rect x="468" y="44" width="148" height="40" rx="4" fill="#e8f5e9" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="542" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Physical custody</text><text x="542" y="76" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="8">KEY # + MEDECO</text>
                        <path d="M136 64H160M280 64H304M444 64H468" stroke="#00859B" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                        <text x="148" y="58" fill="#00859B" font-size="8">mand.</text>
                        <text x="16" y="110" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Room also participates in Work Assignment. Key holder is a role during custody — not a separate entity.</text>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="help-links">
                    <a asp-page="/Administration/WorkforceMembers/Index">Workforce Members</a>
                    <a asp-page="/Administration/WorkAssignments/Index">Work Assignments</a>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="key-types" class="help-section">
                <h3>Key types</h3>
                <p>Key Types classify access patterns at the KEY # level. Create types under Catalog → Key Types, or enter a new type when registering a KEY #. Retire a type when it should no longer be used; delete only when no KEY # references it.</p>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Catalog/KeyTypes">Key Types</a></div>
            </section>

            <section id="key-medeco" class="help-section">
                <h3>KEY # &amp; MEDECO</h3>
                <table class="help-matrix">
                    <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><strong>KEY #</strong></td><td>Shared access number. Associated with the set of Rooms that open. Many physical copies may share one KEY #.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>MEDECO Key Code</strong></td><td>Identifies the specific physical key copy issued to a person. Unique within a KEY #; may repeat under a different KEY #.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><strong>Room #</strong></td><td>Operator-facing room identifier.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <div class="help-diagram-frame" role="img" aria-label="KEY # 66800 hierarchy: opens Room 410D; MEDECO copies 26, 27, 28">
