                        <rect x="116" y="96" width="72" height="28" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="152" y="114" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">411A</text>
                        <rect x="208" y="96" width="72" height="28" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="244" y="114" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">412B</text>
                        <rect x="300" y="96" width="72" height="28" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="336" y="114" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">420C</text>
                        <path d="M210 68V96M60 96V80H336" stroke="#5E6A7D" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <p class="help-diagram-note">Find by Room # returns every KEY # that opens that room — including MASTER1 for each room it opens. No special master-key search path.</p>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Catalog/KeyRooms">KEY # Rooms</a></div>
            </section>

            <section id="registering-keys" class="help-section">
                <h3>Registering keys</h3>
                <p>From Catalog → Register Key:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Ensure a Key Type exists (or enter a new one).</li>
                    <li>Create the <strong>KEY #</strong> (shared access number).</li>
                    <li>Assign <strong>Room #</strong> openings to that KEY #.</li>
                    <li>Register each <strong>MEDECO</strong> physical copy under that KEY #.</li>
                </ol>
                <div class="help-links">
                    <a asp-page="/Catalog/Register">Register Key</a>
                    <a asp-page="/Catalog/Keys">Browse Keys</a>
                </div>
            </section>
        </article>

        <article id="operate" class="help-chapter">
            <h2>Operate</h2>

            <section id="issuing" class="help-section">
                <h3>Issue a key</h3>
                <p>Hand an available MEDECO physical copy to an eligible person. Prerequisites: active workforce member with department, at least one active work assignment, and an available MEDECO copy under a KEY #.</p>
                <ol class="help-steps">
                    <li>Search <strong>Key holder</strong> by name or UIN — eligible matches only; nothing is preselected.</li>
                    <li>Select the holder deliberately.</li>
                    <li>Select <strong>KEY #</strong>, then an <strong>available MEDECO</strong> copy (MEDECO stays empty until KEY # is chosen).</li>
                    <li>Confirm <strong>Rooms opened</strong> shown as derived from the KEY # — do not re-enter rooms.</li>
                    <li>Choose For = Department or Room and the matching justification (no default).</li>
                    <li>Confirm Issued / Due as operator local times.</li>
                    <li>Enter <strong>Loan code</strong> (required).</li>
                    <li>Issue Key — next Issue opens clean.</li>
                </ol>
                <div class="help-diagram-frame" role="img" aria-label="Issue flow: holder, KEY #, MEDECO, derived rooms, justification, loan code">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 480 72" width="480" height="72" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
