                        <path d="M210 64V80M80 80V68H340" stroke="#5E6A7D" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Operations/Receive">Receive Key</a></div>
            </section>

            <section id="finding" class="help-section">
                <h3>Find Key</h3>
                <p>One search box accepts <strong>KEY #</strong>, <strong>MEDECO</strong>, <strong>Key Type</strong>, or <strong>Room #</strong>. Matching uses the same partial-match style across those dimensions.</p>
                <p>Searching a Room # returns every KEY # that opens that room (including multi-room master KEY # values), with each MEDECO copy’s availability and current holder.</p>
                <p><strong>Questions Find answers:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>What Room # values does KEY # 66800 open?</li>
                    <li>What MEDECO copies exist under KEY # 66800? Which are available or issued?</li>
                    <li>Who holds MEDECO 28 under KEY # 66800?</li>
                    <li>Which KEY # values open Room X? (search by that Room #)</li>
                    <li>Which KEY # / MEDECO a person currently holds? (Member Keys / Details / Keys by Member report)</li>
                </ul>
                <figure class="help-figure">
                    <img class="help-shot" src="~/images/help/04-find-key.png" alt="Find Key results showing KEY #, MEDECO, rooms opened, availability, and current holder" />
                    <figcaption>Find Key — search by KEY #, MEDECO, Key Type, or Room #.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Operations/Find">Find Key</a></div>
            </section>
        </article>

        <article id="govern" class="help-chapter">
            <h2>Govern</h2>

            <section id="lifecycle" class="help-section">
                <h3>Lifecycle &amp; corrections</h3>
                <p>Operators may correct authorized business records. Lifecycle rules vary by entity — edit where mutable; delete only when unused and unreferenced; otherwise retire, end, or terminate.</p>
                <div class="help-lifecycle-strip">
                    <article><h4>Delete</h4><p>Permanent removal. Only when no governed relationships or history block it.</p></article>
                    <article><h4>Retire</h4><p>Preserve the record and history while preventing future operational use.</p></article>
                    <article><h4>Terminate</h4><p>End a Workforce Member’s operational lifecycle.</p></article>
                    <article><h4>End</h4><p>End a Work Assignment relationship.</p></article>
                    <article><h4>Activate</h4><p>Restore a retired record where supported.</p></article>
                    <article><h4>Remove</h4><p>Remove a governed relationship such as KEY # ↔ Room.</p></article>
                </div>
                <div class="help-diagram-frame" role="img" aria-label="Lifecycle paths: unused may delete; used may retire, end, or terminate; retired may activate; relationships may be removed">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 680 150" width="680" height="150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                        <rect x="4" y="4" width="672" height="142" rx="8" fill="#F5F7FA" stroke="#D9DEE8"/>
                        <text x="16" y="22" fill="#00205B" font-size="11" font-weight="700">HELP-DIAGRAM-07 · Record lifecycle</text>
                        <rect x="20" y="40" width="140" height="36" rx="4" fill="#e8f5e9" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="90" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Unused / unreferenced</text>
                        <rect x="200" y="40" width="140" height="36" rx="4" fill="#e6f4f7" stroke="#00859B"/><text x="270" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Used / referenced</text>
                        <rect x="380" y="40" width="100" height="36" rx="4" fill="#e8eef7" stroke="#00205B"/><text x="430" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#0B1F3A" font-size="10">Retired</text>
                        <rect x="520" y="40" width="140" height="36" rx="4" fill="#F5F7FA" stroke="#5E6A7D" stroke-dasharray="4 2"/><text x="590" y="62" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="10">Relationship</text>
                        <text x="90" y="96" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Edit where mutable</text>
                        <text x="90" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Delete where authorized</text>
                        <text x="270" y="96" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Edit where mutable</text>
                        <text x="270" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Retire / Terminate / End</text>
                        <text x="430" y="96" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Activate where supported</text>
                        <text x="590" y="96" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Remove / End</text>
                        <text x="590" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">by relationship semantics</text>
                        <text x="16" y="136" fill="#5E6A7D" font-size="9">Actions differ by record type — use the matrix below for the record in front of you.</text>
                    </svg>
                </div>
                <table class="help-matrix">
                    <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Edit</th><th>Delete</th><th>Lifecycle</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>Department</td><td>Code</td><td>Unused only</td><td>Retire when referenced; Activate yes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Room</td><td>Room # / description</td><td>Unused only</td><td>Retire where permitted; Activate yes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Workforce Member</td><td>Details</td><td>Unused only</td><td>Terminate (no generic Retire)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Work Assignment</td><td>Governed primary</td><td>Active unused where allowed</td><td>End</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Key Type</td><td>—</td><td>When no KEY #</td><td>Retire / Activate</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>KEY #</td><td>—</td><td>No copies / room relationships</td><td>Retire / Activate</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>MEDECO</td><td>—</td><td>When no loan history</td><td>Retire / Activate</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>KEY # ↔ Room</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>Remove relationship</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </section>

            <section id="audit" class="help-section">
                <h3>Audit Trail</h3>
                <p>See who performed which business action. Filter by date, operator, action, or subject; export CSV, Excel, or PDF of the filtered result. Available filters may be a subset of all recorded actions.</p>
                <p><strong>Example audit entries:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Key issued</li>
                    <li>Key returned</li>
                    <li>Department code changed</li>
                    <li>KEY # created</li>
                    <li>Physical key copy registered</li>
                    <li>KEY # ↔ Room assignment added or removed</li>
                </ul>
                <figure class="help-figure">
                    <img class="help-shot" src="~/images/help/05-audit-trail.png" alt="Audit Trail list with date, operator, action, subject, and details columns with filter controls" />
                    <figcaption>Audit Trail — operator business mutations with export.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Administration/AuditTrail">Audit Trail</a></div>
            </section>

            <section id="reports" class="help-section">
                <h3>Reports &amp; exports</h3>
                <p>Filter on screen, then download <strong>CSV</strong>, <strong>Excel</strong>, or <strong>PDF</strong>. Timestamps in exports use readable <code>yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm UTC</code> form; on-screen lists use friendly local presentation.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/CurrentKeyHolders">Current Key Holders</a> — who holds each issued key now</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/KeysByWorkforceMember">Keys by Member</a> — issued keys and return history for one person</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/ActiveLoans">Active Loans</a> — all currently issued keys</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/OverdueKeys">Overdue Keys</a> — open loans past due</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/KeyHistory">Key History</a> — issue and return history for one key</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/OutstandingByWorkforceStatus">Outstanding by Status</a> — members who still hold keys</li>
                    <li><a asp-page="/Reports/KeyCatalog">Key Catalog</a> — registered keys and Available/Issued state</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="help-links"><a asp-page="/Reports/Index">All Reports</a></div>
            </section>

            <section id="blockers" class="help-section">
                <h3>Common blockers</h3>
                <div class="help-blockers">
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>Cannot find person at Issue</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Inactive member, missing Work Assignment, or search terms that do not match.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Verify an active Workforce Member with a valid Work Assignment, then search by name or UIN.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>No MEDECO available</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>No physical copies registered, or all copies are currently issued or unavailable.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Register a MEDECO copy under the KEY #, or return an open issue.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>Cannot issue</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Governed readiness or eligibility prerequisites are incomplete.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Use the contextual resolution links on Issue Key — do not invent a separate checklist here.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>Cannot delete Department</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Governed relationships or history block permanent removal.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Retire the department when Delete is unavailable.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>Cannot return</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>No matching open loan, or the wrong physical copy is selected.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Select the open KEY # / MEDECO issue on Receive Key.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                    <article class="help-blocker">
                        <h4>KEY # missing expected Room</h4>
                        <dl>
                            <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The Room is not assigned to that KEY #.</dd>
                            <dt>What to do</dt><dd>Assign the Room under Catalog → KEY # Rooms.</dd>
                        </dl>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

